{{--
  Privacy notice (plan §22.7) — code-defined, owned by the Landing module.

  TEMPLATE COPY. It describes what this codebase actually stores and who it
  shares it with, but it is not legal advice and it names no company. Replace
  the bracketed parts, have it reviewed, and remove the notice at the top
  before launch.
--}}
@component('layouts/marketing', {
  title: 'Privacy notice',
  description: `How ${appName} collects, uses and protects personal data.`,
})
  <article class="content-article">
    <div class="info-box info-box-warning" style="margin-bottom: 32px">
      Template text. Replace the bracketed details and have this reviewed before launch.
    </div>

    <header class="content-article-header">
      <h1 class="content-article-title">Privacy notice</h1>
      <div class="content-article-meta">Last updated [date]</div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This notice explains what personal data {{ appName }} ("we") collects when you use the
        service, why, and what you can do about it. The controller is [company name, address].
        Contact us at [privacy contact email].
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account details</strong> — your name, email address, and a hash of your password (never the password itself). If you sign in with Google or GitHub, the identifier and email they give us.</li>
        <li><strong>Workspace data</strong> — what you and your colleagues create in the product, and the files you upload.</li>
        <li><strong>Billing records</strong> — your plan and payment history. Card details are handled by our payment provider and never reach us.</li>
        <li><strong>Security and usage records</strong> — sign-in times, IP addresses and an audit trail of significant actions, kept to protect your account and the service.</li>
        <li><strong>Support conversations</strong> — the tickets you open and their attachments.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>Only the providers that run the service for us, under contract:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>[Payment provider] — our merchant of record, which processes payments and sales tax.</li>
        <li>[Email provider] — delivers account and notification emails.</li>
        <li>[Storage provider] — stores uploaded files.</li>
        <li>[Hosting provider] — runs the application and its database.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell personal data, and we do not use it for advertising.</p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use a session cookie to keep you signed in and a security token to protect forms. We do
        not use advertising or tracking cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        [Describe retention periods.] Billing records are kept as long as the law requires, even
        after an account is closed.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, export or delete
        your personal data, and to object to how it is used. Contact [privacy contact email] and we
        will respond within [period].
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If we change this notice in a way that matters, we will tell you in the app before it takes effect.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
@end
